  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about getting your interior walls painted? Knowing what to expect can really help you feel prepared and confident. The process usually kicks off with clearing and protecting the room. This means moving furniture, covering floors, and masking off areas not being painted. Then, it's all about prepping the walls themselves. This involves cleaning them thoroughly, filling any minor cracks or nail holes, and a bit of light sanding to ensure a smooth surface. If there are significant repairs or a drastic color change, priming might be necessary to get the best adhesion and an even color. After all that careful prep, the finish coats go on. Most professional jobs will involve at least two coats to ensure rich, consistent color. Throughout the process, communication is key! A good contractor, like HH Remodeling LLC, will keep you in the loop on progress and any questions that come up. Finally, it’s all about the cleanup, which includes removing all coverings, putting furniture back (if agreed upon), and ensuring the space is spotless. Typically, a professional can complete a room in one or two days, depending on its size and the condition of your walls. It’s a pretty straightforward process when handled by experienced pros, designed to minimize disruption and maximize results."
    }
  ],
